<a name="Web"></a>
<h1>ADA Technical Accommodations</h1>
<p>It is the goal of the 2nd Judicial Circuit to provide all users with a functional, accessible and interactive Web experience.</p>
 
<p>If you use assistive technology (such as a Braille reader, a screen reader, TTY, 
etc.) and the format of any 
of our web site material interferes with your 
ability to access the information, please contact the ADA Coordinator, Regina Shaw, at 850-606-4401, or via email <a href="mailto:ShawR@leoncountyfl.gov">ShawR@leoncountyfl.gov,</a> to be provided with further assistance.</p> 

<p>To enable us to respond in a manner most helpful to you, please indicate your disability type,
the preferred format for return correspondence, the web address of the requested material and your contact information. </p>
 
<h4>Recommendations for Enhancing Accessibility</h4>
<p>We recommend that users download the latest version of 
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.adobe.com/products/acrobat/readstep2.html">Adobe Reader</a>
to view PDF files: 

Version 7.0 and higher of this software is available
 and provides a number of features that improve access for users. 
 For further information please visit:
<a target="_blank" href="http://access.adobe.com/">http://access.adobe.com/</a></p>
